      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.respondToWebhook",
      "typeVersion": 1.1,
      "position": [860, 160],
      "id": "a1f0c2d4-8888-4a0b-9c31-000000000008",
      "name": "Respond - answer"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "The routing field `escalated` is a **boolean emitted by the service**, produced by `src/escalation.py` reading the generated answer.\n\nIt is not a substring match on prose, and it does not change the generator: `GENERATION_SYSTEM` and `GENERATION_PARAMS` are the constants held identical across the three benchmark runs.\n\nMeasured against the judge on configurations it was not written on: 1 missed escalation of 37 rows, 0 wrong escalations of 155. The split is by configuration rather than by question, so the genuinely unseen evidence is **3 of 4 answers** - see `docs/escalation-detector.md`.\n\nStrict type validation is on. A response without a boolean `escalated` errors the node rather than falling through to the answer branch.",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 400,
        "color": 4
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [400, 260],
      "id": "a1f0c2d4-9999-4a0b-9c31-000000000009",
      "name": "Sticky Note - how routing works"
    }
  ],
